Required:
Claude API key for end point or use any local modals

Steps to run:
1. Navigate to bin folder, create a script folder and paste the .jmx files there
2. Inside the scripts folder create a new folder and name it as results: On running the script it will store the aggregate report, summary report, logs and debug
3. Open the command prompt or terminal. navigate to the jmeter bin folder:
cd C:\Users\Prakash.Manoharan\Downloads\apache-jmeter-5.6.3\apache-jmeter-5.6.3\bin>
4. Run this command:
.\jmeter.bat -n -t scripts\sampleRequest.jmx  -Dclaude.api.key=sk-ant-YOU_API_KEY -Dthreads=1 -Drampup=2 -Dduration=30 -l scripts\results\summary.csv -j scripts\results\jmeter.log

This command contains the number of thread to run, rampup period and the duration in seconds. Also it contains locations to save the results + logs.

